// saoirse 
Narrator: You learn that the girls who were stuck are called Ada and Ondine, who were checking the stores in the underground caves before the incident.
Ada: It’s a good thing that rock only blocked the entries… nothing important was damaged, but we’ll need to start moving the supplies out soon. #portrait:Ada
Ondine: Or somehow get that rock off without damaging anything else.
Narrator: It’s surprising how full the beach feels when everyone’s gathered here together.
Narrator: There are less ‘proper’ buildings compared to the settlements inland. But maybe that has to do with their everyday life?
Saorise: You’re the ones who brought in that boat, aren’t you? #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: Thank you for your help. #portrait:Saorise
Narrator: Your gaze trails to Ada and Ondine, who are being fussed over and scolded for thinking about work right after a near-death experience. 
Narrator: Laughter and relieved smiles abound.
Noelle: It’s no problem. Lives were at risk, after all. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Zale: There you guys are! Saorise, shouldn’t we help them repair their boat? #portrait:Zale
Zale: It kinda got messed up because of us. #portrait:Zale
Zale: …Speaking of, I haven’t seen you around before. Are you a new Krakenfolk from the humans? #portrait:Zale
Narrator: After you explain your situation, the two share a look — but it seems like Zale is waiting for Saorise to give an answer.
Saorise: Let me introduce myself formally. My name is Saorise, and I’m what you could call the chief of this village. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: We can definitely give you access to some of our artifact collections, but there’s an even more urgent matter… #portrait:Saorise
Narrator: At you and Amelia’s looks of confusion, she smiles.
Saorise: It seems like you still don’t know how to swim. #portrait:Saorise
